==Latin==
===Etymology=== 
From {{etyl|itc-pro|la}} {{m|la|*flek-t|||}}, of {{unk.|title=uncertain|lang=la}} ultimate origin, lacking any solid Indo-European cognates.  Possible {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} predecessors include {{m|ine-pro|*bʰleK-||}}, {{m|ine-pro|*dʰleK-||}}, and {{m|ine-pro|*gʷʰleK-||}}.
===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈflek.toː/|lang=la}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|flecto|flectō|flectere|flectere|flexi|flexī|flexum|flexum}}

# I [[bend]], [[curve]] or [[bow]].
# I [[turn]] or [[curl]].
# {{context|figuratively|lang=la}} I [[persuade]], [[prevail]] upon, or [[soften]].

